# Canvas registry contract (S14) — `apps/web/src/canvas/registry.ts`

Consumers: S15 (`pdf`), S15b (`generated_media`). S14 ships `document`, `diagram`, `table`, `chart`, `video`.

## Server side (what the tool emits)
`open_in_canvas(kind, ref)` and any tool that wants the canvas emit a custom block
`{"type": "block", "block": {"type": "canvas", "data": CanvasRef}}` and the composed message keeps the same
`CanvasRef` in `state.canvas[]` (so a reopened thread restores it from the checkpoint).

```ts
/** What the canvas shows. JSON-serialisable; never carries an unattempted question's answer fields. */
export interface CanvasRef {
  /** Unique per thread (server-assigned, e.g. "cv_3f2a…"); the panel replaces an open item with the same key. */
  key: string;
  /** Registered kind: "document" | "diagram" | "table" | "chart" | "video" | (S15) "pdf" | (S15b) "generated_media". */
  kind: string;
  /** Who wrote it: "assistant" renders violet; "student" renders paper (e.g. after Keep). */
  origin: "assistant" | "student";
  /** ui_copy key for the panel title, or null to use `title`. */
  title_key: string | null;
  /** Plain-text title chosen by the tool (escaped, ≤ 120 chars); the client never renders it as HTML. */
  title: string | null;
  /** Server-side id of the thing shown, when it lives in a table (note id, media_assets id, pdf upload id ...). */
  ref: { type: string; id: string } | null;
  /** Kind-specific payload, validated by the kind's zod schema on the client before rendering. */
  data: Record<string, unknown>;
}
```
Kind payloads in S14: `document` {doc: TipTap JSON (S06 node schema), anchor?: {type, id}}; `diagram` {mermaid: string (server-validated)};
`table` {columns: [{key, label_key|label}], rows: [...]}; `chart` {chart: "bar"|"line", x: string, series: [...], rows: [...]}; `video` {media_id, provider:"youtube", video_id, start_s?}.

## Client registry
```ts
import type { ComponentType } from "react";
import type { ZodType } from "zod";

export interface CanvasKindProps<D = Record<string, unknown>> {
  item: CanvasRef & { data: D };
  /** Close this item (panel stays open if others remain). */
  close(): void;
  /** Replace this item in place (e.g. document "Keep" flips origin to "student" and sets ref). */
  update(next: Partial<CanvasRef>): void;
}

export interface CanvasKind<D = Record<string, unknown>> {
  kind: string;
  /** Validates `item.data`; an item that fails renders the shared error state (canvas.invalid), never crashes. */
  schema: ZodType<D>;
  /** Lazy component; loaded only when an item of this kind opens. */
  load(): Promise<{ default: ComponentType<CanvasKindProps<D>> }>;
  /** ui_copy key used when the item has neither title_key nor title (e.g. "canvas.kind.pdf"). */
  label_key: string;
  /** Lucide icon name for the tab chip. */
  icon: string;
  /** Feature flag that must be on (public-config feature_flags) or the kind is ignored. */
  requires_flag?: string;
}

/** Register a kind; returns unregister. Same `kind` twice → the later registration wins (HMR-safe). */
export function registerCanvasKind<D>(spec: CanvasKind<D>): () => void;
export function getCanvasKind(kind: string): CanvasKind | undefined;
/** Open / focus an item (from a block, a button or a page). */
export function openInCanvas(ref: CanvasRef): void;
export function useCanvas(): { items: CanvasRef[]; active: string | null; open; close; update; focus };
```
- S15: `registerCanvasKind({kind: "pdf", requires_flag: "library", ...})` from `apps/web/src/canvas/kinds/pdf.ts` (you own that file); register it in `apps/web/src/canvas/kinds/index.ts` (one line; I'll accept the PR-style edit, just tell me on the ledger).
- S15b: same with `generated_media` (label "AI-generated" chip is part of your component).
- Layout (side panel ≥ 1100 px and iPad landscape, full-screen sheet otherwise), close/tab chrome, violet/paper framing and the error/empty states are the registry's, not the kind's.
